[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1595850444","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011#issuecomment-1595850444","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011","id":1595850444,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85fHr7M","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-06-17T20:18:03Z","updated_at":"2023-06-20T18:34:06Z","body":"I didn't look at this too closely but I'm not sure this should be seen as an \"exception\" in the SPDX sense. It claims to be a section 7 additional term but this seems to refer to the language authorizing use of additional terms \"[d]eclining to grant rights under trademark law for use of some trade names, trademarks, or service marks\" which does not concern additional permissions (which is how SPDX understands exceptions for purposes of the exception list). \r\n\r\nHowever, the language in the LICENSE file basically just says \"the licensing of the Program under the AGPL does not imply a trademark license\" and references a separate trademark policy which grants certain permissions to use the \"Z-PUSH\" mark. \r\n\r\nAlso, to be clear, this package is not in Fedora and therefore I don't think the \"major distro\" qualifier should apply here (EDIT: as a result of a connection to Fedora) unless SPDX wants to treat RPMFusion itself as a major distro.  \r\n \r\nOne further point: The AGPL additional terms I remember from Zarafa when it was packaged in Fedora were different from what's here. Those were basically badgeware terms, were the result of a negotiation between Red Hat and Zarafa lawyers, and I think today Fedora would probably not allow such terms. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1595850444/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1595867147","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011#issuecomment-1595867147","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011","id":1595867147,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85fHwAL","user":{"login":"robert-scheck","id":10982488,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwOTgyNDg4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10982488?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/robert-scheck","html_url":"https://github.com/robert-scheck","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robert-scheck/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robert-scheck/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robert-scheck/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robert-scheck/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robert-scheck/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robert-scheck/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robert-scheck/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robert-scheck/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robert-scheck/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-06-17T21:36:07Z","updated_at":"2023-06-17T21:36:07Z","body":"> Also, to be clear, this package is not in Fedora and therefore I don't think the \"major distro\" qualifier should apply here unless SPDX wants to treat RPMFusion itself as a major distro.\r\n\r\nI'm not sure what qualifies as \"major distro\", but as of writing Z-Push is shipped with Debian (main) and Ubuntu (universe), too.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1595867147/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1595931697","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011#issuecomment-1595931697","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011","id":1595931697,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85fH_wx","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-06-18T02:45:54Z","updated_at":"2023-06-18T02:45:54Z","body":"Ah, I would think if it's in Debian main it should qualify as \"major distro\", yes, but that's up to the SPDX legal team. I was mainly concerned that someone unfamiliar with RPMFusion might assume this package is in Fedora.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1595931697/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1601943256","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011#issuecomment-1601943256","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011","id":1601943256,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85fe7bY","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-06-22T02:50:10Z","updated_at":"2023-06-22T02:50:10Z","body":"Debian qualifies for \"used in major distro\"\r\n\r\nfor ease of reference, will paste text in comments","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1601943256/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1601943588","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011#issuecomment-1601943588","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011","id":1601943588,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85fe7gk","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-06-22T02:50:51Z","updated_at":"2023-06-22T02:52:15Z","body":"from https://github.com/Z-Hub/Z-Push/blob/develop/LICENSE#L666 - key text in italics, as rest is standard AGPL-3.0 header\r\n\r\nCopyright 2007 - 2016 Zarafa Deutschland GmbH\r\n\r\nThis program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify\r\nit under the terms of the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3,\r\nas published by the Free Software Foundation _with the following additional\r\nterm according to sec. 7:_\r\n\r\n_According to sec. 7 of the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3,\r\nthe terms of the AGPL are supplemented with the following terms:_\r\n\r\n_\"Zarafa\" is a registered trademark of Zarafa B.V.\r\n\"Z-Push\" is a registered trademark of Zarafa Deutschland GmbH\r\nThe licensing of the Program under the AGPL does not imply a trademark license.\r\nTherefore any rights, title and interest in our trademarks remain entirely with us._\r\n\r\n_Our trademark policy (see TRADEMARKS) allows you to use our trademarks\r\nin connection with Propagation and certain other acts regarding the Program.\r\nIn any case, if you propagate an unmodified version of the Program you are\r\nallowed to use the term \"Z-Push\" to indicate that you distribute the Program.\r\nFurthermore you may use our trademarks where it is necessary to indicate the\r\nintended purpose of a product or service provided you use it in accordance\r\nwith honest business practices. For questions please contact Zarafa at\r\ntrademark@zarafa.com._\r\n\r\nThis program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful,\r\nbut WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied warranty of\r\nMERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the\r\nGNU Affero General Public License for more details.\r\n\r\nYou should have received a copy of the GNU Affero General Public License\r\nalong with this program.  If not, see <http://www.gnu.org/licenses/>.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1601943588/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1601952595","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011#issuecomment-1601952595","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011","id":1601952595,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85fe9tT","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-06-22T03:05:27Z","updated_at":"2023-06-22T03:05:27Z","body":"@richardfontana FWIW This (or something similar) was on our \"more research needed\" list for Fedora license data. There was a listing for \"Affero General Public License 3.0 with Zarafa trademark exceptions\" and the Fedora shortname, \"AGPLv3 with exceptions (as @robert-scheck already noted) on the old wiki \"good list\". It had a link that's now dead at http://www.zarafa.com/content/affero-gplv3 - since I couldn't find the actual text of the exception, it didn't get matched and added to the new Fedora-license-list data. \r\nUsing Wayback Machine, I found a similar but different than the text above version from 2014: http://web.archive.org/web/20140214025000/http://www.zarafa.com/content/affero-gplv3\r\nby the Wayback Machine capture in mid-2015 and 2016, it gives the same 404 as today.\r\nNot sure what to do with that info... but FWIW!\r\n\r\nAs for whether this should be an exception on the SPDX License List, I know there was lengthy discussions on how to deal with a potential onslaught of additional clauses under GPL-3.0, section 7. That would apply to AGPL-3.0 as well. I'd have to dig into the email archive to remember any outcomes (other than there not being an onslaught) and it may very well have even pre-dated 2.0 when we added a separate exception list... \r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1601952595/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1601995514","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011#issuecomment-1601995514","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011","id":1601995514,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85ffIL6","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-06-22T04:30:48Z","updated_at":"2023-06-22T04:30:48Z","body":"@jlovejoy additional clauses under GPLv3 section 7 (in the sense I'm pretty sure you mean) are conceptually not \"exceptions\" in the SPDX exception list sense - they are not additional permissions. Additional permissions (corresponding to traditional GPLv2 \"exceptions\") are covered in a different part of GPLv3 section 7. I know this case shows how odd this is because in a sense it seems like this is mostly a grant of trademark *permission*. The relevant part of GPLv3 section 7 was meant to legitimize simple clauses like \"This license does not grant you any rights to use licensor's trademarks\".","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1601995514/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1601996834","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011#issuecomment-1601996834","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011","id":1601996834,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85ffIgi","user":{"login":"richardfontana","id":1179636,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExNzk2MzY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1179636?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana","html_url":"https://github.com/richardfontana","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/richardfontana/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-06-22T04:33:35Z","updated_at":"2023-06-22T04:33:35Z","body":"In my opinion this is an appropriate case for 'AdditionRef-' and is not appropriate for addition to the SPDX exception list under the current criteria. ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1601996834/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1649638818","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011#issuecomment-1649638818","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011","id":1649638818,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85iU32i","user":{"login":"swinslow","id":678569,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3ODU2OQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/678569?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow","html_url":"https://github.com/swinslow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/swinslow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-07-25T11:18:08Z","updated_at":"2023-07-25T11:18:08Z","body":"I tend to agree with @richardfontana on this. This seems closer to general \"additional terms\" that would be referenced using a custom \"AdditionRef-\" identifier as discussed [here](https://github.com/spdx/change-proposal/issues/4#issuecomment-1526155230).\r\n\r\nI don't think this would meet the exception requirements for the [SPDX Exceptions List](https://spdx.org/licenses/exceptions-index.html), since to the extent it's granting additional rights, they appear to be trademark rights as dictated by Zarafa's corporate trademark policy. I think that's specific to Zarafa and is outside the scope of what would be counted as an \"exception\" for Exception List purposes.","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1649638818/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1666043737","html_url":"https://github.com/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011#issuecomment-1666043737","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/2011","id":1666043737,"node_id":"IC_kwDOA0JFE85jTc9Z","user":{"login":"jlovejoy","id":5048659,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwNDg2NTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5048659?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy","html_url":"https://github.com/jlovejoy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jlovejoy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2023-08-04T18:53:16Z","updated_at":"2023-08-04T18:53:16Z","body":"sounds good, I'll close then\r\n\r\n@robert-scheck - I'm not sure Fedora has documented the use of `AdditionRef-` yet as it's new in SPDX (and actually not officially part of the spec yet). If there isn't a corresponding issue in Fedora's Gitlab repo yet, please make one and @richardfontana  and I will respond there :)","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/spdx/license-list-XML/issues/comments/1666043737/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]